1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,921
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,006
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:43,961
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:47,089
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:49,007
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:54,429
PREVIOUSLY

7
00:00:54,513 --> 00:00:57,182
[distorted voice] Detective Jin,
did you think the game was over?

8
00:00:57,266 --> 00:00:58,267
Round 2.

9
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:04,314
[glass shattering]

10
00:01:05,649 --> 00:01:07,234
Detective Jin, you got lucky.

11
00:01:08,193 --> 00:01:10,988
For now, I think we should move
Detective Jin to a safe house.

12
00:01:11,071 --> 00:01:13,782
[Changun] Put Team 1 with him.
You can trust them.

13
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:16,159
[scoffs]

14
00:01:17,494 --> 00:01:19,538
[Isoo] It's a box I've never seen before.

15
00:01:23,041 --> 00:01:24,418
[timer beeping]

16
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:27,045
-What?
-It's a bomb!

17
00:01:27,129 --> 00:01:28,422
[tires screeching]

18
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:29,923
What's going on?

19
00:01:30,007 --> 00:01:33,260
There's a bomb in the car.
Blast radius is 50... No, 100 meters.

20
00:01:33,343 --> 00:01:34,469
Take the wheel.

21
00:01:34,553 --> 00:01:35,929
[tires screeching]

22
00:01:36,722 --> 00:01:38,098
[Hyera] Four minutes left.

23
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,142
[Isoo] I know a place.

24
00:01:46,315 --> 00:01:47,774
[siren blaring]

25
00:01:50,444 --> 00:01:51,570
[grunts]

26
00:01:55,324 --> 00:01:56,533
[grunts]

27
00:01:59,494 --> 00:02:01,079
[Hyera] There are people here. Be careful.

28
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:06,001
[car horn honking]

29
00:02:06,084 --> 00:02:07,210
[grunts]

30
00:02:07,294 --> 00:02:10,047
[car horn honking]

31
00:02:13,342 --> 00:02:14,509
[tires screeching]

32
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:17,888
-Detective Park, stop!
-[tires screech]

33
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:19,431
[siren blaring]

34
00:02:22,059 --> 00:02:23,185
[tires screech]

35
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:31,693
[tires screech]

36
00:02:32,694 --> 00:02:34,154
-Nine seconds.
-Open the door.

37
00:02:35,238 --> 00:02:36,740
-What?
-Open the door!

38
00:02:41,912 --> 00:02:43,246
[timer continues beeping]

39
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:52,839
Three, two, one!

40
00:02:57,594 --> 00:02:58,595
[grunts]

41
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:00,138
[heavy thud]

42
00:03:08,939 --> 00:03:10,023
[groans]

43
00:03:15,278 --> 00:03:18,323
[muffled explosion]

44
00:03:23,829 --> 00:03:25,580
[both panting]

45
00:03:31,211 --> 00:03:32,295
[Hyera grunts softly]

46
00:03:34,131 --> 00:03:35,507
[Isoo grunts]

47
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:37,050
[Hyera grunts]

48
00:03:40,887 --> 00:03:41,888
[exhales sharply]

49
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:45,892
[both continue panting]

50
00:03:46,768 --> 00:03:48,478
[car approaching]

51
00:03:48,562 --> 00:03:50,439
-[tires screech]
-[car door opens]

52
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:51,523
[Kyungjin] Bro!

53
00:03:55,068 --> 00:03:56,903
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.

54
00:03:56,987 --> 00:03:58,738
That was way too close.

55
00:03:58,822 --> 00:03:59,823
Are you all right?

56
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:01,324
Yes.

57
00:04:02,284 --> 00:04:05,454
We need a different location.
I don't know how far ahead they planned.

58
00:04:05,537 --> 00:04:07,497
[vehicles approaching]

59
00:04:09,374 --> 00:04:11,251
[siren blaring]

60
00:04:14,212 --> 00:04:16,548
Get Detective Jin out of here
before backup arrives.

61
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:18,049
Understood.

62
00:04:20,677 --> 00:04:21,678
You're okay, right?

63
00:04:22,554 --> 00:04:23,555
Yes.

64
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:25,849
[Junyoung exhales sharply]

65
00:04:27,434 --> 00:04:29,644
Violent Crimes' car exploded?

66
00:04:29,728 --> 00:04:31,188
-Yes, sir.
-[gasps]

67
00:04:31,772 --> 00:04:34,024
You mean, the bomber came
to the police station

68
00:04:34,107 --> 00:04:36,318
and planted a bomb in our car?

69
00:04:36,401 --> 00:04:38,570
-[sighs softly]
-This is a nightmare.

70
00:04:39,446 --> 00:04:41,031
What are we going to do?

71
00:04:41,114 --> 00:04:43,283
The press is waiting.

72
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:44,951
So what?

73
00:04:45,869 --> 00:04:48,163
-You handle it.
-Sir.

74
00:04:49,414 --> 00:04:52,083
Don't look at me.
Go out there and deal with it!

75
00:04:52,167 --> 00:04:53,877
[scoffs] I can't believe this.

76
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:56,046
[breathing heavily]

77
00:04:56,129 --> 00:04:57,589
[♪ tense music playing]

78
00:04:57,672 --> 00:04:59,341
[reporters chattering]

79
00:05:01,051 --> 00:05:02,427
[reporter 1] Can you tell us
what happened?

80
00:05:02,511 --> 00:05:04,304
We heard a police vehicle had exploded.

81
00:05:04,387 --> 00:05:05,931
[reporter 2] Was
Detective Jin Isoo inside?

82
00:05:06,014 --> 00:05:07,057
[reporter 3] Any casualties?

83
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:09,184
-[reporter 4] Did you catch them?
-Who's behind this?

84
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:11,728
[reporters clamoring]

85
00:05:14,231 --> 00:05:15,232
[clamor subsides]

86
00:05:15,315 --> 00:05:16,566
There are no casualties.

87
00:05:16,650 --> 00:05:20,487
We'll place this case under embargo
until the investigation is complete.

88
00:05:21,071 --> 00:05:22,405
[reporter 5] Embargo?

89
00:05:22,489 --> 00:05:24,699
We've already had
two large-scale explosions.

90
00:05:25,826 --> 00:05:28,286
We don't know what the culprit is after.

91
00:05:29,287 --> 00:05:30,872
We can't risk provoking them.

92
00:05:31,581 --> 00:05:32,582
Please cooperate.

93
00:05:32,666 --> 00:05:34,668
[clamor resumes]

94
00:05:52,352 --> 00:05:53,770
[Isoo sighs]

95
00:05:55,313 --> 00:05:57,190
Where are we?

96
00:05:58,775 --> 00:06:00,777
The safest place we have right now.

97
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:05,156
Let's go inside.

98
00:06:15,876 --> 00:06:17,127
[Isoo sighs]

99
00:06:26,344 --> 00:06:28,138
ECSTASY
A BREATHLESS FALL

100
00:06:28,221 --> 00:06:30,307
CLIMAX
LIGHT SCATTERED ACROSS THE UNIVERSE

101
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:32,350
DISSOLUTION
THE SILENCE OF WHISPERING REEDS

102
00:06:32,434 --> 00:06:34,603
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

103
00:06:41,568 --> 00:06:43,904
What's with the decor here? Huh?

104
00:06:48,867 --> 00:06:49,910
MS. JOO HYERA

105
00:06:49,993 --> 00:06:51,995
-Is this Joo Hyera's place?
-Yeah.

106
00:06:52,078 --> 00:06:53,622
The bomber would never expect it.

107
00:06:53,705 --> 00:06:54,789
[Isoo] Yeah.

108
00:06:54,873 --> 00:06:57,167
I didn't expect it either.
I'm going to a hotel.

109
00:06:57,250 --> 00:06:58,376
Hey, come on. Why?

110
00:06:58,460 --> 00:07:00,587
Because she embarrassed me on national TV,

111
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:03,632
and she keeps bossing me around
like she's our team leader.

112
00:07:03,715 --> 00:07:05,050
Hey, Jin Isoo.

113
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:09,512
She offered up her home to keep you safe.
Stop being so petty.

114
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,723
[Kyungjin] He's right. You should rest.

115
00:07:11,806 --> 00:07:13,433
You've had a really stressful day.

116
00:07:14,225 --> 00:07:15,560
Where's the bedroom?

117
00:07:15,644 --> 00:07:17,062
It's this way. Come on, bro.

118
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:18,480
[Isoo sighs in exasperation]

119
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:20,106
[Kyungjin] God, we need a team leader.

120
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:21,232
This way, bro.

121
00:07:23,234 --> 00:07:24,319
[Isoo sighs]

122
00:07:33,036 --> 00:07:34,037
[scoffs]

123
00:07:36,414 --> 00:07:38,541
That evil woman
likes cute things like this?

124
00:07:44,756 --> 00:07:46,549
[grunting]

125
00:07:49,135 --> 00:07:50,512
Why're you lying on the floor?

126
00:07:50,595 --> 00:07:52,389
I don't sleep in other people's beds.

127
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:53,640
Go. I'm going to sleep.

128
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:06,861
Night, bro.

129
00:08:11,241 --> 00:08:12,242
[door closes]

130
00:08:15,495 --> 00:08:16,663
What about Isoo?

131
00:08:16,746 --> 00:08:18,039
He went to sleep.

132
00:08:18,123 --> 00:08:19,916
Okay. Good job today.

133
00:08:19,999 --> 00:08:22,043
You go back to the station.
I'll stay here.

134
00:08:22,127 --> 00:08:23,294
Got it.

135
00:08:27,090 --> 00:08:28,091
[sighs]

136
00:08:34,556 --> 00:08:36,099
MISSED CALL
JIWON

137
00:08:36,683 --> 00:08:37,851
[sighs]

138
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:44,858
INCOMING CALL
JIWON

139
00:08:44,941 --> 00:08:46,192
[cell phone vibrating]

140
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:48,361
Hello? Jiwon, sorry--

141
00:08:48,445 --> 00:08:50,363
[Dr. Yoon] What happened?
Are you okay? Where are you?

142
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:52,657
Uh, Jiwon.

143
00:08:52,741 --> 00:08:55,076
Calm down. One question at a time.

144
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:58,455
How can I be calm?
A car exploded at the Hangang River.

145
00:08:59,039 --> 00:09:00,957
Isoo's unharmed.

146
00:09:01,041 --> 00:09:03,209
-We're now at a safe house, so--
-And you?

147
00:09:03,293 --> 00:09:04,294
What?

148
00:09:04,377 --> 00:09:06,171
Are you okay?

149
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:08,798
I was really worried.

150
00:09:11,926 --> 00:09:14,721
Yes, I'm completely fine.

151
00:09:15,346 --> 00:09:16,514
[sighs in relief]

152
00:09:20,185 --> 00:09:21,811
Do you know how scared I was?

153
00:09:23,605 --> 00:09:25,648
Who on earth would do something like this?

154
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:27,650
Exactly.

155
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:31,738
This is the third incident now.
I'm sure we'll find some evidence.

156
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:35,241
I need Team 2 to go over the footage
from the launch event again.

157
00:09:35,325 --> 00:09:37,535
Let me know if you see
any suspicious movements.

158
00:09:37,619 --> 00:09:39,162
[in English] Okay. [in Korean] Come on.

159
00:09:39,788 --> 00:09:40,914
-[detective 1] Okay.
-[detective 2] Okay.

160
00:09:44,793 --> 00:09:46,878
Let's check
the parking lot security footage.

161
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:47,962
Got it.

162
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:51,841
[sighs softly]

163
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:54,010
[mouse clicks]

164
00:09:54,094 --> 00:09:56,012
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

165
00:10:07,065 --> 00:10:08,108
[music fades]

166
00:10:19,911 --> 00:10:21,162
[groans softly]

167
00:10:21,246 --> 00:10:22,247
[cell phone vibrates]

168
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:31,089
[distorted voice, in English] Final Round.

169
00:10:31,172 --> 00:10:33,383
[♪ foreboding music playing]

170
00:10:41,641 --> 00:10:43,893
[in Korean] Come alone.
He'll blow up if I see anyone else.

171
00:10:45,145 --> 00:10:46,604
You know where this is.

172
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:51,192
MR. CHOI

173
00:10:51,776 --> 00:10:53,194
[line ringing]

174
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:01,119
[automated voice] The number
you have dialed...

175
00:11:01,202 --> 00:11:04,539
[music swells, fades]

176
00:11:08,877 --> 00:11:10,170
[keyboard clacks]

177
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:12,797
[sighs heavily] Did you find anything?

178
00:11:13,381 --> 00:11:14,382
No.

179
00:11:14,883 --> 00:11:16,801
No one approached the vehicle.

180
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:20,680
Then how did they put the bomb in there?

181
00:11:21,639 --> 00:11:23,266
When was the vehicle last used?

182
00:11:23,349 --> 00:11:24,684
Three days ago.

183
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:28,646
Let's check the nearby dashcams
in the morning.

184
00:11:28,730 --> 00:11:29,856
Okay.

185
00:11:29,939 --> 00:11:30,940
By the way,

186
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:33,443
what about Park Gyeongtae?

187
00:11:33,526 --> 00:11:35,403
[♪ ominous music plays]

188
00:11:38,781 --> 00:11:41,701
We've been watching him,
but he never left his house.

189
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:43,119
[sighs]

190
00:11:43,703 --> 00:11:45,830
My team will retrieve
the vehicle tomorrow.

191
00:11:46,956 --> 00:11:48,666
-Go get some shut-eye.
-Okay.

192
00:11:52,462 --> 00:11:53,588
[sighs softly]

193
00:12:04,307 --> 00:12:05,350
[sighs heavily]

194
00:12:16,444 --> 00:12:17,654
[cell phone snaps shut]

195
00:12:29,749 --> 00:12:31,751
[♪ gripping music playing]

196
00:12:36,297 --> 00:12:37,715
[shower running]

197
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:09,080
NEARBY PARKED VEHICLE RECORDS

198
00:13:09,163 --> 00:13:10,415
[music fades]

199
00:13:12,458 --> 00:13:14,752
[line connects, ringing]

200
00:13:16,254 --> 00:13:18,798
Yes, sir.
Sorry for disturbing you so early.

201
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:20,466
I couldn't reach you yesterday.

202
00:13:21,843 --> 00:13:24,012
You parked in front
of a Violent Crimes vehicle.

203
00:13:24,846 --> 00:13:26,973
I need to check your dashcam footage.

204
00:13:27,557 --> 00:13:30,268
Yes, please call me when you arrive.
I'll come up to get it.

205
00:13:32,395 --> 00:13:33,396
[line disconnects]

206
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:36,566
-I'll contact the rest of the list.
-Okay.

207
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:52,206
Sorry, I left on my own.

208
00:13:53,708 --> 00:13:55,251
Even if I end up dead,

209
00:13:56,002 --> 00:13:57,378
you guys are not at fault.

210
00:13:59,255 --> 00:14:01,382
Park Junyoung, Choi Kyungjin...

211
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,760
Thanks for everything.

212
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:06,679
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

213
00:14:07,263 --> 00:14:08,765
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

214
00:14:08,848 --> 00:14:09,849
-Good luck.
-Thanks.

215
00:14:14,187 --> 00:14:15,188
Hey, here you go.

216
00:14:15,271 --> 00:14:16,814
-Thank you.
-Take care.

217
00:14:16,898 --> 00:14:17,899
Yes, sir.

218
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:27,366
THIRD INCIDENT
POLICE VEHICLE BOMB ATTACK

219
00:14:30,995 --> 00:14:32,663
HIGH-YIELD AMMONIUM NITRATE IED

220
00:14:32,747 --> 00:14:34,332
100-METER BLAST RADIUS

221
00:14:34,415 --> 00:14:36,042
[music intensifies]

222
00:14:43,508 --> 00:14:44,675
[♪ music fades]

223
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:01,484
[♪ tense music playing]

224
00:15:02,777 --> 00:15:04,028
[sighs in exasperation]

225
00:15:08,116 --> 00:15:11,035
[line connects, ringing]

226
00:15:11,119 --> 00:15:14,497
[cell phone vibrating]

227
00:15:16,749 --> 00:15:18,251
[automated voice] The number
you have dialed...

228
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:20,461
[sighs wearily] Isoo.

229
00:15:24,257 --> 00:15:25,633
[cell phone vibrating]

230
00:15:26,134 --> 00:15:27,135
Hello?

231
00:15:27,885 --> 00:15:28,886
What?

232
00:15:30,054 --> 00:15:31,055
Understood.

233
00:15:33,099 --> 00:15:35,101
-What's wrong?
-Isoo disappeared.

234
00:15:36,602 --> 00:15:38,980
-Did he take Detective Park's car?
-I think so.

235
00:15:40,314 --> 00:15:43,276
-I'll head out now. You track him down.
-Got it.

236
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:49,615
[engine revving]

237
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:04,088
There he is.
Please track license plate 9832.

238
00:16:04,172 --> 00:16:05,173
[officer] Got it.

239
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:17,935
[cell phone ringing]

240
00:16:19,145 --> 00:16:21,772
-[Kyungjin] Ma'am.
-Yes, where's Detective Jin?

241
00:16:21,856 --> 00:16:24,400
Near his family estate.
The address is 251 Pyeongjin-dong.

242
00:16:24,483 --> 00:16:26,569
I'll head over there, so keep me updated.

243
00:16:26,652 --> 00:16:28,988
-And let Detective Park know, too.
-Yes, ma'am.

244
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:44,712
[♪ foreboding music playing]

245
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:55,514
[panting]

246
00:16:55,598 --> 00:16:57,225
What are you doing here?

247
00:17:00,478 --> 00:17:01,896
I got a DM.

248
00:17:01,979 --> 00:17:04,523
I was told to come here and film you die.

249
00:17:05,775 --> 00:17:07,526
GO FILM HIM DIE
BE THERE, OR ELSE

250
00:17:07,610 --> 00:17:08,611
It's my mom.

251
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:12,573
[cell phone vibrates]

252
00:17:14,325 --> 00:17:16,494
[distorted voice] Head inside together.

253
00:17:18,371 --> 00:17:19,622
We're being watched.

254
00:17:21,624 --> 00:17:22,625
Let's go inside.

255
00:17:28,965 --> 00:17:29,966
Mr. Choi!

256
00:17:42,853 --> 00:17:43,938
[cell phone vibrates]

257
00:17:45,648 --> 00:17:47,066
[distorted voice] Turn on the camera.

258
00:17:47,149 --> 00:17:49,068
Unless you want to see your mom die.

259
00:17:49,902 --> 00:17:51,988
[♪ enthralling music playing]

260
00:18:21,642 --> 00:18:22,768
[cell phone vibrates]

261
00:18:23,644 --> 00:18:24,812
[music fades]

262
00:18:26,856 --> 00:18:27,857
Turn around.

263
00:18:30,067 --> 00:18:31,986
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

264
00:18:45,249 --> 00:18:48,377
[gasps in fear] Detective! Detective Jin!

265
00:18:48,461 --> 00:18:49,462
Over here.

266
00:18:59,722 --> 00:19:03,476
There's a bomb in the car.
Blast radius is 50... No, 100 meters.

267
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:07,229
[Isoo] Follow me.

268
00:19:10,650 --> 00:19:12,777
[grunts] There's a bunker here.

269
00:19:13,402 --> 00:19:14,445
[gasps in disbelief]

270
00:19:15,321 --> 00:19:16,447
[timer beeping]

271
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:18,866
[clangs]

272
00:19:18,949 --> 00:19:20,284
[metallic creak]

273
00:19:21,285 --> 00:19:22,662
-[cell phone vibrates]
-Hello?

274
00:19:22,745 --> 00:19:24,538
He's at Jin Myeongchul's house.

275
00:19:24,622 --> 00:19:26,290
I think Jin Isoo has been set up.

276
00:19:26,374 --> 00:19:27,958
[sighs]

277
00:19:28,042 --> 00:19:30,252
Please alert local police
and emergency services.

278
00:19:30,336 --> 00:19:31,420
I will.

279
00:19:31,504 --> 00:19:33,464
-Be careful.
-Yes, sir.

280
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,927
[Hyeonwoo panting frantically]

281
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:40,721
[timer continues beeping]

282
00:19:40,805 --> 00:19:42,932
[continues panting]

283
00:19:51,565 --> 00:19:53,192
It should've gone off by now.

284
00:20:05,162 --> 00:20:06,288
[mouse clicking]

285
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:09,583
[camera chimes]

286
00:20:11,794 --> 00:20:13,587
[Hyeonwoo breathing heavily]

287
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:20,720
[keyboard clacking]

288
00:20:22,054 --> 00:20:24,140
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

289
00:20:30,521 --> 00:20:32,106
That bastard was bluffing.

290
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:34,608
[scoffs]

291
00:20:38,237 --> 00:20:39,280
[gasps in horror]

292
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:40,656
Detective!

293
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:42,116
[panting frantically]

294
00:20:44,827 --> 00:20:46,245
[timer beeping]

295
00:20:47,121 --> 00:20:48,706
[music intensifies, fades]

296
00:20:54,712 --> 00:20:55,921
[tires screech]

297
00:20:58,048 --> 00:20:59,133
[engine shuts off]

298
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:03,929
[explosion]

299
00:21:04,013 --> 00:21:05,931
[♪ tense music playing]

300
00:21:12,021 --> 00:21:13,022
Detective Jin!

301
00:21:15,107 --> 00:21:16,358
Jin Isoo, where are you?

302
00:21:38,088 --> 00:21:40,674
-[footsteps approaching]
-[Isoo sighs in relief]

303
00:21:40,758 --> 00:21:42,426
[coughs] Over here.

304
00:21:45,304 --> 00:21:47,556
Are you okay? What happened?

305
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:50,226
[panting]

306
00:21:51,018 --> 00:21:52,770
Why is the Assistant Director here?

307
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:56,482
It's a long story.
Let's get out of here first.

308
00:21:56,565 --> 00:21:58,984
[hurried footsteps approaching]

309
00:21:59,068 --> 00:22:00,069
Hey.

310
00:22:01,445 --> 00:22:02,446
You okay?

311
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:06,033
[sighs wearily]

312
00:22:06,575 --> 00:22:07,701
You asshole!

313
00:22:09,328 --> 00:22:10,329
You...

314
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:12,331
If something had happened to you...

315
00:22:12,414 --> 00:22:14,792
I didn't have a choice.
Let's get out of here first.

316
00:22:16,544 --> 00:22:17,545
[grunts in frustration]

317
00:22:34,311 --> 00:22:36,939
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

318
00:22:41,861 --> 00:22:43,404
[sirens blaring]

319
00:22:48,659 --> 00:22:49,952
[brakes squeal]

320
00:22:51,537 --> 00:22:53,205
[Isoo] It was because of this.

321
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:01,297
But he wasn't here?

322
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:03,507
No.

323
00:23:04,675 --> 00:23:06,427
[sighs] Then what could've happened?

324
00:23:07,177 --> 00:23:08,596
[Hyera] Was he taken somewhere else?

325
00:23:09,138 --> 00:23:10,764
Maybe the photo was just a bait.

326
00:23:11,599 --> 00:23:13,517
The photo was definitely taken here.

327
00:23:17,396 --> 00:23:18,522
[Kyungjin] Chairman Choi is here.

328
00:23:20,816 --> 00:23:22,234
-[Isoo] Mr. Choi.
-Yes.

329
00:23:22,818 --> 00:23:23,903
Are you all right?

330
00:23:24,486 --> 00:23:25,571
Did you get hurt?

331
00:23:25,654 --> 00:23:27,406
What about you?

332
00:23:27,489 --> 00:23:28,616
Where were you?

333
00:23:29,199 --> 00:23:31,035
I was traveling by helicopter.

334
00:23:31,118 --> 00:23:33,037
Then how did you know to come here?

335
00:23:33,120 --> 00:23:36,415
You didn't answer when I called you back,
so I contacted Detective Choi.

336
00:23:37,082 --> 00:23:38,459
[sighs softly]

337
00:23:42,713 --> 00:23:44,131
You should call your mother.

338
00:23:48,052 --> 00:23:50,095
[line connects, ringing]

339
00:23:51,430 --> 00:23:54,391
Hello? Mom, where are you?
Why didn't you answer your phone?

340
00:23:54,475 --> 00:23:56,060
At the sauna?

341
00:23:56,810 --> 00:23:58,854
God, Mom! I really can't with you.

342
00:23:58,938 --> 00:24:00,439
-I'm hanging up.
-[line disconnects]

343
00:24:01,023 --> 00:24:02,816
So this was just a deepfake.

344
00:24:03,651 --> 00:24:06,362
Then why bomb this place?
Using a fake photo, no less.

345
00:24:08,614 --> 00:24:09,990
To kill me.

346
00:24:15,287 --> 00:24:16,956
We should go. It's too dangerous.

347
00:24:17,539 --> 00:24:18,624
[Hyera] Wait.

348
00:24:21,627 --> 00:24:23,253
You said the bomber's watching.

349
00:24:24,797 --> 00:24:27,174
[ticking]

350
00:24:29,301 --> 00:24:31,095
[♪ tense music playing]

351
00:24:31,178 --> 00:24:33,430
[onlookers murmuring]

352
00:24:45,943 --> 00:24:48,862
[♪ ominous music plays]

353
00:24:48,946 --> 00:24:50,823
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

354
00:24:50,906 --> 00:24:54,493
The unexploded bomb was defused on site,
and it's currently being analyzed.

355
00:24:54,576 --> 00:24:55,577
FORENSICS

356
00:24:55,661 --> 00:24:57,621
[♪ soft suspenseful music playing]

357
00:25:04,420 --> 00:25:06,797
[Hyera] Jang Hyeonwoo is hiding out
at a nearby motel.

358
00:25:08,924 --> 00:25:11,135
[coughing]

359
00:25:11,719 --> 00:25:13,470
And I've relocated Detective Jin.

360
00:25:14,430 --> 00:25:15,556
Where?

361
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:17,141
[birds chirping]

362
00:25:18,892 --> 00:25:21,311
[♪ serene music playing]

363
00:25:21,395 --> 00:25:23,147
[Isoo exclaims in satisfaction]

364
00:25:23,230 --> 00:25:24,940
I haven't been over in so long.

365
00:25:25,024 --> 00:25:26,400
[grunts]

366
00:25:29,069 --> 00:25:31,613
[Mr. Choi] Go wash up.
I'll make you something to eat.

367
00:25:31,697 --> 00:25:32,990
In a minute.

368
00:25:33,782 --> 00:25:35,576
[chuckles] Quickly, come on.

369
00:25:36,076 --> 00:25:37,536
There you go. [grunts]

370
00:25:38,746 --> 00:25:39,872
[exhales deeply]

371
00:25:43,167 --> 00:25:44,168
[chuckles softly]

372
00:25:46,545 --> 00:25:48,505
[Isoo exclaims in satisfaction]

373
00:25:48,589 --> 00:25:51,425
This house seems too small
for the chairman of the Hansu Group.

374
00:25:51,508 --> 00:25:52,885
Do you want a bigger place?

375
00:25:53,761 --> 00:25:55,137
I like it here.

376
00:25:55,220 --> 00:25:56,388
And I like you, Mr. Choi.

377
00:25:56,472 --> 00:25:58,057
[chuckles]

378
00:25:58,140 --> 00:25:59,141
Have a seat.

379
00:26:00,225 --> 00:26:01,435
[sighs contentedly]

380
00:26:04,938 --> 00:26:06,732
CHOI JEONGHUN

381
00:26:07,483 --> 00:26:08,692
Are you unwell?

382
00:26:10,194 --> 00:26:12,780
No, it's just a little indigestion.

383
00:26:13,739 --> 00:26:15,449
Did you get it checked out?

384
00:26:15,532 --> 00:26:16,533
I will.

385
00:26:17,159 --> 00:26:18,160
Go on.

386
00:26:19,161 --> 00:26:20,746
[chair clatters]

387
00:26:22,498 --> 00:26:24,083
[breathes deeply]

388
00:26:24,166 --> 00:26:25,793
I haven't had porridge in a while.

389
00:26:27,086 --> 00:26:28,128
Mmm.

390
00:26:28,212 --> 00:26:29,880
-[Mr. Choi] How is it?
-It's seasoned perfectly.

391
00:26:29,963 --> 00:26:31,340
-Just as I expected.
-[chuckles]

392
00:26:31,423 --> 00:26:34,760
Mmm. Mmm.

393
00:26:34,843 --> 00:26:37,012
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

394
00:26:50,734 --> 00:26:52,111
We got a partial print.

395
00:26:52,611 --> 00:26:54,279
Submit it for expedited analysis.

396
00:26:54,363 --> 00:26:55,614
It's really urgent.

397
00:26:56,406 --> 00:26:58,408
-Did they find something?
-[Hyera] Yes.

398
00:26:58,492 --> 00:27:00,327
A partial print. It'll take a while.

399
00:27:01,954 --> 00:27:02,955
FOURTH INCIDENT

400
00:27:04,957 --> 00:27:07,543
Four bomb attacks,
but only one partial fingerprint.

401
00:27:08,127 --> 00:27:11,463
We should've found something
at the event site or the parking lot.

402
00:27:12,089 --> 00:27:13,757
Anything on the security footage?

403
00:27:15,300 --> 00:27:18,679
We checked all the parking lot cameras
and dashcams.

404
00:27:18,762 --> 00:27:20,848
Everything up to two days
before the incident.

405
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:25,936
[exhales heavily]

406
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:31,733
It wasn't here.

407
00:27:32,818 --> 00:27:34,361
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

408
00:27:35,737 --> 00:27:39,116
No one's bold enough
to plant a bomb at a police station.

409
00:27:41,451 --> 00:27:44,079
-You went to the first site in that car?
-Yes.

410
00:27:45,289 --> 00:27:47,207
They lured you there to plant the bomb.

411
00:27:49,001 --> 00:27:50,460
I'll get their security footage.

412
00:27:58,635 --> 00:28:00,304
ANONYMOUS TIPSTER

413
00:28:01,638 --> 00:28:02,723
[Isoo sighs]

414
00:28:04,516 --> 00:28:06,059
Who could be behind all this?

415
00:28:08,061 --> 00:28:09,229
[sighs deeply]

416
00:28:09,313 --> 00:28:10,731
Yeah, who could it be?

417
00:28:10,814 --> 00:28:12,274
Who would want me...

418
00:28:14,318 --> 00:28:15,861
[high-pitched ringing]

419
00:28:15,944 --> 00:28:18,322
[♪ pensive music playing]

420
00:28:20,032 --> 00:28:21,450
[Junyoung] Don't touch that!

421
00:28:21,533 --> 00:28:23,577
-[exhales, grunts]
-[timer beeping rapidly]

422
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:25,996
[distorted voice] Come alone.
He'll blow up if I see anyone else.

423
00:28:27,247 --> 00:28:28,415
[groans in pain]

424
00:28:28,498 --> 00:28:30,083
-[muffled bang]
-[high-pitched ringing continues]

425
00:28:30,167 --> 00:28:31,877
-[Mr. Choi] What's wrong?
-Detective!

426
00:28:31,960 --> 00:28:33,670
-[glass shattering]
-[muffled explosion]

427
00:28:33,754 --> 00:28:35,130
[Isoo exhales sharply]

428
00:28:36,590 --> 00:28:37,883
[distant tinkling]

429
00:28:37,966 --> 00:28:39,134
[grunts in pain]

430
00:28:40,260 --> 00:28:42,095
-[music stops]
-Drink this.

431
00:28:43,680 --> 00:28:44,681
[grunts]

432
00:28:45,223 --> 00:28:46,224
[gulps]

433
00:28:47,809 --> 00:28:48,936
[exhales shakily]

434
00:28:49,853 --> 00:28:50,854
Are you all right?

435
00:28:51,438 --> 00:28:52,439
[panting] Yeah.

436
00:28:52,940 --> 00:28:54,274
I just...

437
00:28:54,358 --> 00:28:55,859
couldn't breathe for a second.

438
00:28:56,568 --> 00:28:57,694
[sighs]

439
00:28:57,778 --> 00:28:59,529
You should go to the hospital.

440
00:28:59,613 --> 00:29:00,656
[pants]

441
00:29:01,323 --> 00:29:02,574
If you go first.

442
00:29:03,408 --> 00:29:05,702
[pants] I'm fine.

443
00:29:09,247 --> 00:29:11,750
[exhales deeply]
I really don't know who it could be.

444
00:29:15,587 --> 00:29:17,965
But why make it so complicated?

445
00:29:18,757 --> 00:29:21,718
Planting bombs at four locations
and even using a deepfake?

446
00:29:23,053 --> 00:29:24,888
Why not just plant it at your house?

447
00:29:33,188 --> 00:29:34,731
[Seungju] It probably isn't revenge.

448
00:29:35,899 --> 00:29:37,025
The Isoo I know

449
00:29:37,818 --> 00:29:40,779
would never make someone
want revenge this badly.

450
00:29:41,822 --> 00:29:42,823
It might be

451
00:29:43,448 --> 00:29:45,409
driven by desire.

452
00:29:48,161 --> 00:29:50,288
-[pops]
-[clangs]

453
00:29:51,707 --> 00:29:53,083
-[timer beeps]
-[explosion]

454
00:29:56,336 --> 00:29:57,963
[gasps] Mr. Choi.

455
00:29:59,131 --> 00:30:00,674
You know my dad's house.

456
00:30:00,757 --> 00:30:02,551
Do you remember it had a bunker?

457
00:30:02,634 --> 00:30:03,969
Yes, of course.

458
00:30:04,970 --> 00:30:07,556
The bomb went off in there,
which is how I survived.

459
00:30:08,056 --> 00:30:09,683
But it blew a hole in the floor.

460
00:30:16,523 --> 00:30:18,859
I got the footage
from Hansu Department Store.

461
00:30:22,988 --> 00:30:24,239
[keyboard clacking]

462
00:30:32,122 --> 00:30:33,790
[mouse clicking]

463
00:30:37,586 --> 00:30:40,380
[sighs] We won't be able to see anything.

464
00:30:43,050 --> 00:30:44,760
We got a match on the fingerprint.

465
00:30:47,637 --> 00:30:51,308
Jang Hyeonsuk. No criminal record.
He works in R&D at Mirae Electronics.

466
00:30:51,391 --> 00:30:52,392
JANG HYEONSUK

467
00:30:54,144 --> 00:30:56,396
-Should we go bring him in?
-Yes.

468
00:30:56,480 --> 00:30:58,148
-Let's go.
-Right.

469
00:31:02,819 --> 00:31:04,780
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

470
00:31:07,407 --> 00:31:09,451
FIRST INCIDENT
HANSU DEPARTMENT STORE

471
00:31:09,534 --> 00:31:12,287
[Hyera] The first bomb
had a simple design.

472
00:31:12,370 --> 00:31:13,914
Its target was Jin Isoo.

473
00:31:17,793 --> 00:31:18,877
SECOND INCIDENT

474
00:31:19,753 --> 00:31:21,338
The second bomb...

475
00:31:21,838 --> 00:31:23,131
[glass shattering]

476
00:31:23,465 --> 00:31:25,550
It was used to prove they meant business.

477
00:31:26,760 --> 00:31:28,178
THIRD INCIDENT
POLICE VEHICLE

478
00:31:28,762 --> 00:31:30,764
The third bomb...

479
00:31:35,310 --> 00:31:37,562
[muffled explosion]

480
00:31:37,646 --> 00:31:41,024
We need a different location.
I don't know how far ahead they planned.

481
00:31:41,608 --> 00:31:44,611
It sent Jin Isoo to a safe house
and isolated him.

482
00:31:44,694 --> 00:31:45,695
FOURTH INCIDENT

483
00:31:45,779 --> 00:31:47,280
The fourth bomb...

484
00:31:47,864 --> 00:31:49,783
It finally tried to kill Jin Isoo,

485
00:31:49,866 --> 00:31:52,828
but failed because there was a bunker
in the house?

486
00:31:56,581 --> 00:31:57,791
[inhales deeply]

487
00:31:58,416 --> 00:32:00,293
No, that's not it.

488
00:32:08,051 --> 00:32:11,638
There were three explosions.
How could there be no casualties?

489
00:32:13,140 --> 00:32:15,058
[music intensifies, fades]

490
00:32:20,814 --> 00:32:23,024
The bomber wasn't trying to kill Jin Isoo.

491
00:32:28,113 --> 00:32:29,114
[door slides open]

492
00:32:29,698 --> 00:32:31,074
[Mr. Choi exhales deeply]

493
00:32:31,158 --> 00:32:32,200
[sharp gasp]

494
00:32:32,993 --> 00:32:35,370
Do you seriously only own suits?

495
00:32:35,954 --> 00:32:37,956
I even go hiking in a suit.

496
00:32:38,456 --> 00:32:40,083
God, you're so buttoned-up.

497
00:32:40,167 --> 00:32:42,043
It's my fashion philosophy.

498
00:32:42,794 --> 00:32:45,797
By the way, where are you going?

499
00:32:46,381 --> 00:32:49,634
[inhales] I think
I know what the bombers are after.

500
00:32:50,594 --> 00:32:52,679
It could be dangerous.

501
00:32:53,430 --> 00:32:55,015
That looks even more dangerous.

502
00:32:57,392 --> 00:32:58,727
This is great!

503
00:32:59,519 --> 00:33:00,604
It's unique.

504
00:33:04,900 --> 00:33:06,693
They weren't trying to kill me.

505
00:33:08,069 --> 00:33:09,446
It was all a ruse.

506
00:33:10,113 --> 00:33:11,781
I'll go catch them.

507
00:33:13,825 --> 00:33:14,951
[sighs]

508
00:33:15,660 --> 00:33:17,787
-[cell phone vibrates]
-Hello?

509
00:33:17,871 --> 00:33:19,414
Yes, Director. This is Joo Hyera.

510
00:33:20,207 --> 00:33:23,168
Whose idea was it to do a feature
on Detective Jin Isoo?

511
00:33:23,251 --> 00:33:25,795
It was Assistant Director Jang Hyeonwoo.

512
00:33:25,879 --> 00:33:27,714
He said he's a fan of Detective Jin.

513
00:33:27,797 --> 00:33:29,424
Right. Okay.

514
00:33:29,507 --> 00:33:31,259
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

515
00:33:32,219 --> 00:33:33,511
-[cell phone snaps shut]
-That was random.

516
00:33:33,595 --> 00:33:35,347
[line connects, ringing]

517
00:33:36,431 --> 00:33:38,266
Hello, this is Joo Hyera.

518
00:33:39,351 --> 00:33:42,103
Could you check
if Jang Hyeonwoo is inside his room?

519
00:33:42,187 --> 00:33:43,355
Yes, right away.

520
00:33:44,231 --> 00:33:45,357
[line disconnects]

521
00:33:55,867 --> 00:33:57,285
[keyboard clacking]

522
00:34:00,705 --> 00:34:02,457
[mouse clicks]

523
00:34:03,750 --> 00:34:05,460
[♪ tense music playing]

524
00:34:08,922 --> 00:34:10,048
[keyboard key clacks]

525
00:34:22,936 --> 00:34:24,854
JANG HYEONSUK

526
00:34:24,938 --> 00:34:26,815
SIBLING JANG HYEONWOO

527
00:34:34,781 --> 00:34:36,032
[digital beeping]

528
00:34:40,453 --> 00:34:42,247
He used the van to block him from view.

529
00:34:43,039 --> 00:34:44,040
Jang Hyeonwoo.

530
00:34:44,958 --> 00:34:45,959
Jang Hyeonsuk.

531
00:34:49,129 --> 00:34:50,630
PYEONGJIN-DONG ESTATE BOMB ATTACK

532
00:34:50,714 --> 00:34:52,173
251 PYEONGJIN-DONG, SEONGBUK-GU

533
00:34:54,301 --> 00:34:57,512
251 PYEONGJIN-DONG, SEONGBUK-GU

534
00:34:57,596 --> 00:34:59,014
[cell phone vibrating]

535
00:35:01,182 --> 00:35:02,183
Hello?

536
00:35:02,767 --> 00:35:04,352
Jang Hyeonwoo's not here.

537
00:35:19,534 --> 00:35:20,869
[cell phone vibrating]

538
00:35:22,454 --> 00:35:23,496
Detective Park.

539
00:35:25,624 --> 00:35:26,708
[Junyoung clicks tongue]

540
00:35:27,709 --> 00:35:31,463
We can't locate Jang Hyeonsuk.
He hasn't shown up for work either.

541
00:35:32,339 --> 00:35:34,716
-Meet me at Jin Myeongchul's house.
-[Junyoung] Got it.

542
00:35:37,385 --> 00:35:38,386
Let's go.

543
00:35:50,065 --> 00:35:51,983
[♪ foreboding music playing]

544
00:35:56,404 --> 00:35:57,405
[tires screech]

545
00:36:02,494 --> 00:36:03,495
Joo Hyera?

546
00:36:04,704 --> 00:36:06,206
What's with the badass look?

547
00:36:06,289 --> 00:36:07,666
It's for mobility.

548
00:36:08,541 --> 00:36:10,585
And you? Are you Indiana Jones?

549
00:36:12,212 --> 00:36:14,130
[sighs sarcastically]
Too bad I don't have a whip.

550
00:36:15,215 --> 00:36:17,133
-What made you come here?
-[inhales deeply]

551
00:36:17,217 --> 00:36:21,930
I just couldn't figure out how
they planted the bomb inside the house.

552
00:36:22,639 --> 00:36:24,683
Unless the Assistant Director
brought it in.

553
00:36:27,852 --> 00:36:29,521
[♪ dramatic music playing]

554
00:36:33,733 --> 00:36:35,193
[panting frantically]

555
00:36:36,569 --> 00:36:37,570
I can do this.

556
00:36:37,654 --> 00:36:38,655
I can do it.

557
00:36:39,531 --> 00:36:40,657
I can do it.

558
00:36:48,456 --> 00:36:50,083
Detective! Detective Jin!

559
00:36:53,670 --> 00:36:54,879
[digital beeping]

560
00:36:56,297 --> 00:36:57,799
[timer beeping]

561
00:36:57,882 --> 00:36:59,551
What about you? How did you know?

562
00:36:59,634 --> 00:37:02,095
We got a fingerprint off the bomb
by the entrance.

563
00:37:02,178 --> 00:37:03,638
It's Jang Hyeonwoo's brother.

564
00:37:03,722 --> 00:37:07,058
They used to live at this address.
And their mother died five years ago.

565
00:37:07,642 --> 00:37:08,768
Oh...

566
00:37:08,852 --> 00:37:11,229
-You're actually pretty sharp.
-[scoffs]

567
00:37:12,105 --> 00:37:14,065
Their target was the bunker, right?

568
00:37:14,149 --> 00:37:15,150
Yes.

569
00:37:15,233 --> 00:37:17,986
The whole thing was a setup
to blow up that place.

570
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:20,530
Because I'm the only one who can open it.

571
00:37:21,197 --> 00:37:24,033
-[grunts] There's a bunker here.
-[clangs]

572
00:37:24,117 --> 00:37:25,744
[metallic creak]

573
00:37:25,827 --> 00:37:27,704
-[gasps in disbelief]
-Mr. Choi told me

574
00:37:27,787 --> 00:37:29,998
that an extremely
wealthy family used to live here.

575
00:37:30,915 --> 00:37:34,753
When their business went under, they sold
the house to my dad 30 years ago,

576
00:37:35,587 --> 00:37:37,255
but for the last two years or so,

577
00:37:37,338 --> 00:37:40,049
that family kept trying
to buy the house back.

578
00:37:40,633 --> 00:37:41,760
What's in this house?

579
00:37:42,343 --> 00:37:44,679
Good question. Shall we go find out?

580
00:38:04,699 --> 00:38:06,201
[muffled voices]

581
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:07,619
[thudding footsteps]

582
00:38:09,078 --> 00:38:10,246
[Hyeonsuk] Hey, I'll grab that end. Move.

583
00:38:11,790 --> 00:38:13,124
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

584
00:38:13,708 --> 00:38:15,126
[whispering] Looks like
they're already here.

585
00:38:19,672 --> 00:38:22,467
-[muffled clattering]
-[muffled chatter continues]

586
00:38:27,972 --> 00:38:29,349
[Hyeonsuk] Okay, lift on three.

587
00:38:31,518 --> 00:38:33,311
[Hyeonwoo and Hyeonsuk grunting]

588
00:38:33,394 --> 00:38:35,396
[Hyeonsuk] Hey, I'll grab that end. Move.

589
00:38:37,482 --> 00:38:39,108
-Lift. One, two, three.
-[both grunting]

590
00:38:40,777 --> 00:38:42,237
-Hyeonsuk!
-Properly.

591
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:44,113
I told you to bring a dolly.

592
00:38:44,197 --> 00:38:45,698
-Okay, okay.
-It's so heavy.

593
00:38:45,782 --> 00:38:48,576
Think this is gold?
How much would it be worth?

594
00:38:48,660 --> 00:38:50,995
Enough to live our dreams, of course.

595
00:38:51,079 --> 00:38:52,163
[both chuckle]

596
00:38:52,247 --> 00:38:54,999
[Hyeonsuk] I'm going to throw
my resignation right in my manager's face.

597
00:38:56,709 --> 00:38:57,710
You?

598
00:38:58,461 --> 00:39:00,839
Me? I want fried chicken.

599
00:39:00,922 --> 00:39:03,091
-Just chicken? Not even omakase?
-So tasty.

600
00:39:08,054 --> 00:39:09,639
[both panting]

601
00:39:09,722 --> 00:39:12,183
-Tie it on nice and tight.
-Okay.

602
00:39:12,267 --> 00:39:14,143
I'll go up first and pull it up.

603
00:39:14,853 --> 00:39:16,104
-Be careful.
-Okay.

604
00:39:24,362 --> 00:39:25,488
[grunts]

605
00:39:25,572 --> 00:39:27,240
[panting]

606
00:39:33,788 --> 00:39:34,914
Give me a minute.

607
00:39:37,375 --> 00:39:38,751
[♪ upbeat jazz music playing]

608
00:39:38,835 --> 00:39:41,045
-[gasps]
-[shushes]

609
00:39:45,717 --> 00:39:47,093
[gasps softly]

610
00:39:47,176 --> 00:39:48,177
[gun cocks]

611
00:39:49,053 --> 00:39:50,597
[exhales] The police.

612
00:39:50,680 --> 00:39:52,390
You came to arrest me.

613
00:39:54,767 --> 00:39:55,894
[exclaims]

614
00:39:58,479 --> 00:39:59,772
Hyeonsuk, I got it!

615
00:39:59,856 --> 00:40:00,982
I'll tie it up!

616
00:40:02,442 --> 00:40:04,611
[Isoo scatting]

617
00:40:07,238 --> 00:40:08,239
Be quiet.

618
00:40:09,365 --> 00:40:10,867
[Isoo humming]

619
00:40:13,119 --> 00:40:15,705
[Hyeonwoo] Hyeonsuk, did you open it?

620
00:40:19,626 --> 00:40:20,627
Come out.

621
00:40:22,086 --> 00:40:23,212
[exhales deeply]

622
00:40:35,266 --> 00:40:37,477
Don't even think about running.

623
00:40:37,560 --> 00:40:39,437
Where would you go anyway? Come here.

624
00:40:40,939 --> 00:40:41,940
Good job.

625
00:40:42,023 --> 00:40:43,691
[grunting]

626
00:40:44,400 --> 00:40:45,944
[grunting]

627
00:40:46,527 --> 00:40:48,237
I'm worn out from pulling that up,

628
00:40:48,321 --> 00:40:50,740
so you can cuff yourself.

629
00:40:50,823 --> 00:40:51,824
Thanks.

630
00:40:52,700 --> 00:40:54,243
What could this be?

631
00:40:54,327 --> 00:40:55,912
Put the cuffs on. It's okay.

632
00:40:58,957 --> 00:41:00,416
[latch rattling]

633
00:41:02,543 --> 00:41:03,544
[thuds]

634
00:41:10,677 --> 00:41:11,844
[lid creaks]

635
00:41:14,973 --> 00:41:16,015
[gasps]

636
00:41:16,099 --> 00:41:17,850
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

637
00:41:18,601 --> 00:41:20,561
What is it? Is it gold?

638
00:41:20,645 --> 00:41:22,313
Or diamonds?

639
00:41:23,648 --> 00:41:24,649
Do you want to know?

640
00:41:27,735 --> 00:41:29,070
I'm not telling you.

641
00:41:29,153 --> 00:41:30,279
[sighs]

642
00:41:33,908 --> 00:41:34,909
[exclaims]

643
00:41:35,660 --> 00:41:36,661
Take them away.

644
00:41:45,878 --> 00:41:47,005
-[scoffs]
-[handcuffs click]

645
00:41:47,088 --> 00:41:48,715
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

646
00:41:56,264 --> 00:41:59,767
[Hyeonwoo] Our dad died of cancer
two years ago,

647
00:42:00,685 --> 00:42:03,354
and he left one final instruction.

648
00:42:04,230 --> 00:42:07,275
That house... [coughs, wheezes]

649
00:42:08,151 --> 00:42:10,111
You and your brother

650
00:42:11,404 --> 00:42:13,406
must get that house back.

651
00:42:15,158 --> 00:42:16,159
In that place...

652
00:42:18,411 --> 00:42:19,787
rests our family's

653
00:42:20,913 --> 00:42:24,375
most valuable possession.

654
00:42:26,669 --> 00:42:27,670
[whimpers]

655
00:42:28,379 --> 00:42:31,090
Just do as I say.

656
00:42:31,758 --> 00:42:32,759
[exhales sharply]

657
00:42:46,230 --> 00:42:47,648
We didn't believe him.

658
00:42:49,233 --> 00:42:52,904
But our relatives who came to the funeral
said something different.

659
00:42:53,571 --> 00:42:55,782
What happened to the treasure?

660
00:42:56,282 --> 00:42:57,283
Treasure?

661
00:42:58,868 --> 00:43:02,121
Father gave it to Hyeonwoo's grandfather,
didn't he?

662
00:43:02,205 --> 00:43:03,414
[elderly woman] Yes.

663
00:43:03,498 --> 00:43:04,999
That house.

664
00:43:05,083 --> 00:43:07,251
Father gave it to him.

665
00:43:07,335 --> 00:43:09,378
The house? The house I was born in?

666
00:43:09,462 --> 00:43:11,881
[sighs] We sold that house years ago.

667
00:43:12,465 --> 00:43:13,841
That house has been sold.

668
00:43:13,925 --> 00:43:14,926
Yes, it's been sold.

669
00:43:16,552 --> 00:43:17,845
When you sold it,

670
00:43:18,387 --> 00:43:20,556
didn't you take out the chest?

671
00:43:20,640 --> 00:43:22,058
What chest?

672
00:43:22,642 --> 00:43:24,143
The treasure chest.

673
00:43:24,227 --> 00:43:27,939
[scoffs] Oh, come on. There's no treasure.

674
00:43:29,941 --> 00:43:31,567
Unless you saw it yourself...

675
00:43:31,651 --> 00:43:32,819
I saw it.

676
00:43:32,902 --> 00:43:35,321
I saw Father bury the chest there.

677
00:43:36,030 --> 00:43:37,406
You saw it too, didn't you?

678
00:43:37,907 --> 00:43:39,117
I did.

679
00:43:39,700 --> 00:43:41,911
In the dead of night,

680
00:43:41,994 --> 00:43:45,331
he secretly buried that chest
by the old well.

681
00:43:46,666 --> 00:43:49,460
It must've been awfully valuable.

682
00:43:50,211 --> 00:43:53,589
He said it should never be lost.

683
00:43:55,383 --> 00:43:59,387
But then a house was built there.

684
00:44:01,973 --> 00:44:04,225
Chairman Jin Myeongchul's house.

685
00:44:07,854 --> 00:44:09,480
What was inside that chest?

686
00:44:13,192 --> 00:44:14,777
Gold.

687
00:44:15,361 --> 00:44:18,656
I told your dad
when I went to visit him in the hospital.

688
00:44:18,739 --> 00:44:20,116
Nonsense.

689
00:44:20,199 --> 00:44:22,160
How many times do I have to tell you?

690
00:44:22,243 --> 00:44:23,870
You two were imagining things.

691
00:44:26,622 --> 00:44:27,707
[softly] Gold.

692
00:44:30,501 --> 00:44:33,337
Even then, I didn't believe it. But...

693
00:44:34,088 --> 00:44:36,382
Buy that house back, no matter the cost.

694
00:44:37,258 --> 00:44:39,427
The chest is still there.

695
00:44:39,510 --> 00:44:42,930
I need to get it
before those brats catch on.

696
00:44:43,014 --> 00:44:44,682
It was mine to begin with.

697
00:44:44,765 --> 00:44:45,975
Jackpot.

698
00:44:46,058 --> 00:44:48,561
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

699
00:44:49,145 --> 00:44:52,190
So, that's why you tried to kill me?

700
00:44:52,273 --> 00:44:54,692
[exclaims] We weren't trying to kill you.

701
00:44:54,775 --> 00:44:58,070
Yeah. We worked so hard
to make sure nobody got hurt.

702
00:44:58,154 --> 00:45:00,114
We set them off when no one was around.

703
00:45:00,198 --> 00:45:01,490
[♪ ominous music plays]

704
00:45:03,701 --> 00:45:05,536
I almost died three times.

705
00:45:05,620 --> 00:45:07,205
-That was all part of--
-[Hyeonwoo] Sorry.

706
00:45:07,288 --> 00:45:08,539
Sorry.

707
00:45:11,626 --> 00:45:12,627
But...

708
00:45:13,252 --> 00:45:15,296
could you just tell us one thing?

709
00:45:16,297 --> 00:45:17,882
What was inside the chest?

710
00:45:21,344 --> 00:45:23,804
We'll serve time, however many years.
So please.

711
00:45:23,888 --> 00:45:25,598
Please tell us just that. Please?

712
00:45:26,515 --> 00:45:27,558
Ah.

713
00:45:29,518 --> 00:45:30,645
Gold.

714
00:45:30,728 --> 00:45:31,771
[gasps]

715
00:45:33,231 --> 00:45:34,357
[breath trembles]

716
00:45:34,440 --> 00:45:35,775
How much was there?

717
00:45:36,359 --> 00:45:38,694
[exhales] Well, at today's gold prices,

718
00:45:38,778 --> 00:45:40,071
around 100 billion won?

719
00:45:40,154 --> 00:45:41,322
[both exclaim excitedly]

720
00:45:41,405 --> 00:45:42,490
[Hyeonwoo] 100 billion won?

721
00:45:44,116 --> 00:45:45,493
[cries joyfully]

722
00:45:50,831 --> 00:45:53,000
-That belongs to us, right?
-Of course, it does.

723
00:45:53,084 --> 00:45:54,293
Of course.

724
00:45:54,377 --> 00:45:56,587
You deserve it
after all you've been through.

725
00:45:56,671 --> 00:45:58,256
It should be a family heirloom.

726
00:45:58,339 --> 00:45:59,966
Can't you show it to us? Just once?

727
00:46:00,049 --> 00:46:01,384
We risked our lives for this.

728
00:46:01,467 --> 00:46:02,677
Please.

729
00:46:02,760 --> 00:46:05,888
It's ours anyway,
so please let us see it just once.

730
00:46:07,723 --> 00:46:09,475
[♪ jaunty music playing]

731
00:46:11,269 --> 00:46:12,353
Hmm.

732
00:46:17,858 --> 00:46:18,859
[grunts]

733
00:46:23,114 --> 00:46:26,492
You worked hard to find this treasure.
You should at least get to see it.

734
00:46:27,827 --> 00:46:29,328
All right.

735
00:46:32,999 --> 00:46:34,375
[both giggle excitedly]

736
00:46:35,543 --> 00:46:37,044
-Wow.
-We're rich now.

737
00:46:38,504 --> 00:46:40,381
-Wow.
-Wait, what is this?

738
00:46:40,923 --> 00:46:41,924
Wait, hold on.

739
00:46:42,008 --> 00:46:43,009
What?

740
00:46:51,058 --> 00:46:52,059
What the...

741
00:46:56,522 --> 00:46:57,523
[in English] Ready...

742
00:46:58,607 --> 00:46:59,608
Action.

743
00:47:00,109 --> 00:47:05,531
[in Korean] It was a treasure chest that
they orchestrated four bombings to get.

744
00:47:06,532 --> 00:47:09,827
What exactly was inside it?

745
00:47:09,910 --> 00:47:11,370
[♪ intriguing music playing]

746
00:47:12,621 --> 00:47:13,831
[creaking]

747
00:47:17,626 --> 00:47:19,962
The treasure they were
so desperate to find

748
00:47:21,505 --> 00:47:22,506
was none other than...

749
00:47:26,385 --> 00:47:28,137
"JANG DEUKSU"

750
00:47:28,220 --> 00:47:30,473
...a record of collaboration
with Imperial Japan.

751
00:47:33,392 --> 00:47:36,520
The bombers' great-grandfather
was Jang Deuksu.

752
00:47:36,604 --> 00:47:39,065
Also known as "The Master of Torture."

753
00:47:39,148 --> 00:47:43,110
He arrested and tortured
hundreds of independence activists

754
00:47:43,194 --> 00:47:45,196
as a pro-Japanese police officer.

755
00:47:45,279 --> 00:47:47,990
While working as an officer,

756
00:47:48,074 --> 00:47:51,619
Jang Deuksu threatened landowners
into handing over their deeds.

757
00:47:51,702 --> 00:47:54,372
These are those very documents.

758
00:47:55,289 --> 00:47:58,626
Jang Deuksu's sons, Kunkuk and Jongkuk,

759
00:47:59,377 --> 00:48:01,837
sold these lands, amassed a fortune,

760
00:48:01,921 --> 00:48:05,174
and went into postwar reconstruction,
which made them extremely wealthy.

761
00:48:06,008 --> 00:48:09,845
They believed their prosperity
would last forever,

762
00:48:11,138 --> 00:48:13,224
but then a troublemaker was born.

763
00:48:13,808 --> 00:48:16,519
Jang Jongkuk's only son
and the father of the bombers,

764
00:48:17,103 --> 00:48:21,482
Jang Myungjun,
failed at every business he tried.

765
00:48:22,400 --> 00:48:25,069
Perhaps this is what they call
justice prevailing.

766
00:48:25,152 --> 00:48:26,320
JUSTICE WILL PREVAIL

767
00:48:26,904 --> 00:48:28,322
But here's the thing.

768
00:48:30,074 --> 00:48:32,118
Before Jang Myungjun died of cancer,

769
00:48:32,201 --> 00:48:36,205
he told his sons to find the chest
their grandfather had left behind.

770
00:48:37,331 --> 00:48:39,333
The two fools who believed him

771
00:48:40,167 --> 00:48:44,296
orchestrated the bombings
to find this chest.

772
00:48:45,339 --> 00:48:46,757
But what they uncovered...

773
00:48:48,050 --> 00:48:49,218
was evidence

774
00:48:49,301 --> 00:48:53,806
that their family collaborated
with Imperial Japan during the occupation.

775
00:48:53,889 --> 00:48:57,393
It is truly a fitting end
for this collaborationist family.

776
00:48:58,561 --> 00:49:01,605
I suppose another name will be added
to the list of collaborators,

777
00:49:02,398 --> 00:49:04,859
which I plan to publish.

778
00:49:04,942 --> 00:49:08,279
This has been Jin Isoo,

779
00:49:09,280 --> 00:49:10,656
a detective for the people.

780
00:49:11,240 --> 00:49:12,908
[cheering]

781
00:49:12,992 --> 00:49:14,910
That's me. That's me, all right.

782
00:49:14,994 --> 00:49:16,370
A round of applause!

783
00:49:17,413 --> 00:49:19,206
What do you think? Amazing, right?

784
00:49:19,290 --> 00:49:20,499
Yes, amazing.

785
00:49:21,083 --> 00:49:22,668
The comments are blowing up.

786
00:49:23,252 --> 00:49:25,963
"Even busting collaborators,
what can't he do?"

787
00:49:26,046 --> 00:49:27,256
"Just how cool is he?"

788
00:49:28,007 --> 00:49:29,133
Wow, amazing.

789
00:49:29,216 --> 00:49:30,676
My God, just look at this.

790
00:49:30,759 --> 00:49:32,511
-Let's get a beer.
-Yes, sir.

791
00:49:32,595 --> 00:49:33,804
This is insane!

792
00:49:33,888 --> 00:49:35,764
-Look at this.
-Yes, you're amazing.

793
00:49:35,848 --> 00:49:37,892
-Look.
-[Junyoung] Come on. Let's go home.

794
00:49:37,975 --> 00:49:40,060
Where are you going? Come on, admire me.

795
00:49:40,144 --> 00:49:42,188
Bro, you're so cool. The best!

796
00:49:42,271 --> 00:49:43,606
Hey, let's go grab a beer.

797
00:49:43,689 --> 00:49:45,232
Sorry, I have a date.

798
00:49:45,316 --> 00:49:47,693
-Hello? Babe?
-Detective Park.

799
00:49:48,527 --> 00:49:49,528
I have plans, too.

800
00:49:49,612 --> 00:49:50,988
You don't have a girlfriend.

801
00:49:51,071 --> 00:49:53,324
Shut up. See you.

802
00:49:53,824 --> 00:49:55,075
Come on.

803
00:49:59,288 --> 00:50:00,372
[sighs softly]

804
00:50:08,422 --> 00:50:09,465
Jiwon.

805
00:50:09,548 --> 00:50:10,633
Surprised?

806
00:50:12,551 --> 00:50:14,178
Have you been waiting here for me?

807
00:50:14,261 --> 00:50:15,262
Yes.

808
00:50:15,346 --> 00:50:17,264
Come on, I found this great place to eat.

809
00:50:17,348 --> 00:50:19,308
There's always a long wait.
We should hurry.

810
00:50:20,559 --> 00:50:21,727
[Dr. Yoon chuckles]

811
00:50:21,810 --> 00:50:23,479
-Weren't you cold?
-I'm fine.

812
00:50:23,979 --> 00:50:26,023
Up for a drink again tonight?

813
00:50:26,857 --> 00:50:28,526
-[Junyoung] Sure.
-[Dr. Yoon] Great!

814
00:50:30,528 --> 00:50:31,695
[chuckles]

815
00:50:31,779 --> 00:50:33,697
I knew it.

816
00:50:35,032 --> 00:50:36,992
[sighs] I'm so lonely.

817
00:50:37,743 --> 00:50:40,829
I don't have anyone
to share this afterglow with.

818
00:50:44,667 --> 00:50:46,544
-Getting off work?
-Yes.

819
00:50:46,627 --> 00:50:48,963
Not sure if you saw the show,

820
00:50:49,046 --> 00:50:50,798
but I gave it one heck of an ending.

821
00:50:50,881 --> 00:50:52,258
[♪ quirky music playing]

822
00:50:52,341 --> 00:50:54,134
[Hyera] I didn't see it. I was too busy.

823
00:50:54,218 --> 00:50:55,844
Yes. Of course, you were.

824
00:50:57,096 --> 00:50:58,556
Guess this is goodbye.

825
00:50:58,639 --> 00:50:59,765
Happy?

826
00:50:59,848 --> 00:51:01,559
My face gives me away every time.

827
00:51:02,393 --> 00:51:05,604
Wishing you the best
with the Counterterrorism Team. Good luck.

828
00:51:06,188 --> 00:51:08,732
Right. You stay out of trouble, too.
Take care.

829
00:51:08,816 --> 00:51:09,817
Okay.

830
00:51:15,155 --> 00:51:16,657
[sighs in relief]

831
00:51:20,369 --> 00:51:21,829
[exhales deeply]

832
00:51:24,498 --> 00:51:25,666
[Changun] Joo.

833
00:51:26,625 --> 00:51:28,252
[in English] Would you like
something to drink?

834
00:51:30,254 --> 00:51:31,255
[in Korean] You did a great job.

835
00:51:31,964 --> 00:51:33,424
You too, sir.

836
00:51:35,467 --> 00:51:39,138
Working with you again
felt like old times.

837
00:51:39,221 --> 00:51:41,223
-[chuckles softly]
-I could really count on you.

838
00:51:41,307 --> 00:51:42,558
Me too.

839
00:51:43,434 --> 00:51:45,561
What did you think of Jin Isoo?

840
00:51:46,520 --> 00:51:47,646
[inhales deeply]

841
00:51:47,730 --> 00:51:49,565
He can be a bit odd,

842
00:51:50,524 --> 00:51:52,109
and he's unpredictable,

843
00:51:53,193 --> 00:51:54,862
but he's got good instincts.

844
00:51:54,945 --> 00:51:56,822
And he's quite serious about the job.

845
00:51:56,905 --> 00:51:58,365
Right?

846
00:51:58,449 --> 00:52:01,452
He's actually a decent detective.

847
00:52:02,786 --> 00:52:05,164
Do you have someone lined up
to lead Team 1?

848
00:52:08,125 --> 00:52:09,376
[inhales deeply]

849
00:52:09,460 --> 00:52:10,502
No. [exhales]

850
00:52:11,337 --> 00:52:12,338
No one.

851
00:52:17,176 --> 00:52:18,385
So I was wondering...

852
00:52:21,597 --> 00:52:22,681
[Isoo humming]

853
00:52:24,224 --> 00:52:26,769
Chief! Want to watch the show with me?

854
00:52:26,852 --> 00:52:28,228
I saw it.

855
00:52:28,312 --> 00:52:30,189
Jin Isoo, a detective for the people.

856
00:52:31,023 --> 00:52:34,026
Oh. You're getting a new team leader
on Monday.

857
00:52:34,109 --> 00:52:36,195
-Tell your team not to be late.
-Team leader?

858
00:52:36,278 --> 00:52:37,821
-Who is it?
-Curious?

859
00:52:37,905 --> 00:52:39,031
You bet.

860
00:52:39,615 --> 00:52:42,201
You'll see.
I brought in a solid detective.

861
00:52:44,411 --> 00:52:46,955
We're getting a new team leader?

862
00:52:47,873 --> 00:52:50,042
How very interesting.

863
00:52:52,169 --> 00:52:54,463
[on TV] I suppose another name will be
added to the list of collaborators,

864
00:52:55,214 --> 00:52:57,716
which I plan to publish.

865
00:52:58,300 --> 00:53:01,053
Apply now to receive yours for free.

866
00:53:02,137 --> 00:53:05,224
This has been Jin Isoo,

867
00:53:06,433 --> 00:53:07,810
a detective for the people.

868
00:53:07,893 --> 00:53:09,478
[chuckles softly]

869
00:53:09,561 --> 00:53:11,021
That nutjob.

870
00:53:12,147 --> 00:53:13,482
[chuckles softly]

871
00:53:18,070 --> 00:53:19,863
[♪ upbeat swing jazz music playing]

872
00:53:21,323 --> 00:53:22,825
[Isoo] Put it on.

873
00:53:22,908 --> 00:53:24,201
You didn't last time.

874
00:53:24,284 --> 00:53:26,036
Your head's on backward. That's it.

875
00:53:26,120 --> 00:53:27,663
Detective Park, wear it.

876
00:53:27,746 --> 00:53:30,290
-[whines]
-Very handsome. Perfect.

877
00:53:30,374 --> 00:53:31,375
Hello!

878
00:53:32,251 --> 00:53:33,752
[crowd cheering]

879
00:53:34,378 --> 00:53:36,380
[Isoo] Hi there! Want a photo?

880
00:53:36,463 --> 00:53:39,758
Okay. One, two, three.

881
00:53:40,259 --> 00:53:42,636
[Junyoung sighs]
He's going overboard again.

882
00:53:42,720 --> 00:53:44,346
[Kyungjin] Come on, it's all good fun.

883
00:53:45,347 --> 00:53:47,182
VIOLENT CRIME TEAM 1
NEW BOSS COMING

884
00:53:48,434 --> 00:53:50,686
Ahh! Post it on social media.

885
00:53:50,769 --> 00:53:51,979
Okay, band.

886
00:53:52,062 --> 00:53:53,063
Let's give it a try.

887
00:53:53,147 --> 00:53:54,898
Just like we practiced. Ready!

888
00:53:56,650 --> 00:53:57,735
[shouts command]

889
00:53:57,818 --> 00:53:59,987
[♪ triumphant brass fanfare playing]

890
00:54:08,537 --> 00:54:09,621
[in English] Stop!

891
00:54:09,705 --> 00:54:10,706
[in Korean] What in the world...

892
00:54:10,789 --> 00:54:12,166
WELCOME, OUR NEW TEAM LEADER

893
00:54:12,249 --> 00:54:14,084
What is all this?

894
00:54:14,168 --> 00:54:15,169
[in Korean] Sir!

895
00:54:16,462 --> 00:54:19,006
Oh, for heaven's sake.

896
00:54:20,382 --> 00:54:21,383
Sir.

897
00:54:21,967 --> 00:54:24,261
Come on, clear all this out.
[exclaims scornfully]

898
00:54:24,720 --> 00:54:25,721
-This was...
-Sir!

899
00:54:25,804 --> 00:54:26,805
Jin Isoo's doing.

900
00:54:26,889 --> 00:54:29,308
It's for my new boss. You know the drill.

901
00:54:30,100 --> 00:54:31,143
Oh.

902
00:54:34,438 --> 00:54:35,647
[chuckles]

903
00:54:35,731 --> 00:54:37,649
-Somebody's working hard.
-[Isoo] Of course.

904
00:54:37,733 --> 00:54:39,610
We're getting a new team leader.

905
00:54:39,693 --> 00:54:40,694
Of course.

906
00:54:40,778 --> 00:54:42,529
-Like the flowers?
-Yeah.

907
00:54:42,613 --> 00:54:45,449
-Oh. Incoming!
-Really? My new boss is here?

908
00:54:46,325 --> 00:54:48,994
[whispering] Okay, here we go.
[shouts command]

909
00:54:51,288 --> 00:54:52,414
[shouts command]

910
00:54:52,498 --> 00:54:54,666
[♪ triumphant brass fanfare playing]

911
00:55:08,931 --> 00:55:10,015
[engine shuts off]

912
00:55:13,477 --> 00:55:14,645
[music stops]

913
00:55:16,980 --> 00:55:18,982
[♪ dramatic music plays]

914
00:55:22,778 --> 00:55:24,488
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

915
00:55:27,741 --> 00:55:28,742
Joo Hyera?

916
00:55:38,085 --> 00:55:39,461
[camera shutters clicking]

917
00:56:07,114 --> 00:56:09,825
-[music fades]
-I didn't expect such a grand welcome.

918
00:56:09,908 --> 00:56:10,993
[chuckles softly]

919
00:56:11,660 --> 00:56:14,454
Detective Jin has been working hard
since morning.

920
00:56:15,372 --> 00:56:16,540
I guess you can be sweet.

921
00:56:17,499 --> 00:56:21,044
This is the new team leader of Violent
Crime Investigation Team 1, Joo Hyera.

922
00:56:22,296 --> 00:56:23,964
She's got years on you boys.

923
00:56:24,548 --> 00:56:27,634
She was on our Violent Crime Team
before moving to Counterterrorism.

924
00:56:27,718 --> 00:56:28,719
[chuckles softly]

925
00:56:28,802 --> 00:56:31,930
Detective Jin,
take good care of your new boss.

926
00:56:33,682 --> 00:56:34,808
Take good care of her.

927
00:56:39,813 --> 00:56:41,148
Detective Jin Isoo,

928
00:56:41,857 --> 00:56:44,610
Detective Park Junyoung,
Detective Choi Kyungjin...

929
00:56:44,693 --> 00:56:46,069
I'm glad to join the team.

930
00:56:48,113 --> 00:56:49,615
[muttering] This has to be a nightmare.

931
00:56:49,698 --> 00:56:50,741
It's real.

932
00:56:51,783 --> 00:56:53,076
Get used to it.

933
00:56:53,660 --> 00:56:55,662
[microphone feedback]

934
00:57:00,709 --> 00:57:02,711
[♪ upbeat pop music playing,
Hersh "Shadows In The Night"]

935
00:57:03,837 --> 00:57:05,422
Looking forward to it, nutjob.

936
00:57:28,904 --> 00:57:30,155
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 2

937
00:57:30,238 --> 00:57:31,490
JIN ISOO AND JOO HYERA MEET AGAIN!

938
00:57:56,098 --> 00:57:59,518
Special Cast.
Kim Uiseong

939
00:58:06,608 --> 00:58:07,693
[Hyera] What's the report about?

940
00:58:07,776 --> 00:58:08,902
[woman] There's a ghost
in the abandoned house.

941
00:58:08,985 --> 00:58:11,446
It's asking us to catch the killer.

942
00:58:11,530 --> 00:58:12,823
Of course I'm not scared.

943
00:58:13,573 --> 00:58:14,866
There's definitely something in there.

944
00:58:14,950 --> 00:58:16,493
[man] You uncovered five bodies?

945
00:58:16,576 --> 00:58:18,453
-I said wait for the warrant.
-I bought the house!

946
00:58:18,537 --> 00:58:21,164
[man] A couple and their son,
a college student, were all murdered.

947
00:58:21,248 --> 00:58:24,000
So the house was abandoned after that,
and then it was used as a burial site.

948
00:58:24,084 --> 00:58:26,837
Police! Please come out, serial killer.

949
00:58:27,546 --> 00:58:28,922
[Hyera] We need to start this case over.

950
00:58:29,005 --> 00:58:31,425
-[muffled] Help me!
-[Isoo] So they're professional killers?

951
00:58:31,508 --> 00:58:33,301
[Hyera] They're methodical and cold.

952
00:58:33,385 --> 00:58:35,053
-There's something here.
-[Isoo] Detective Joo.

953
00:58:35,137 --> 00:58:36,263
Just stay close to me from now on.

954
00:58:36,346 --> 00:58:37,514
The hero never dies that easily.

955
00:58:37,597 --> 00:58:38,807
Meow.

956
00:58:39,808 --> 00:58:41,518
Jin Isoo! Nutjob!

957
00:58:41,601 --> 00:58:43,854
-Yes, ma'am!
-[Hyera] We don't know who attacked us.

958
00:58:43,937 --> 00:58:45,939
-Is there a fire?
-[Isoo] No one's going to die.

959
00:58:46,022 --> 00:58:47,107
Why are you being so dramatic?

960
00:58:47,190 --> 00:58:50,527
There's a fire. The detectives
went inside, but now it's on fire.

961
00:58:50,610 --> 00:58:51,987
How do we get out?

962
00:58:53,113 --> 00:58:55,824
-Hey, Jin Isoo.
-[Isoo] I'm working on it!

963
00:58:55,907 --> 00:58:56,992
Get out of the way.

964
00:59:01,121 --> 00:59:03,373
[♪ pensive music playing]

965
00:59:35,655 --> 00:59:37,199
DISSOLUTION

966
01:00:03,517 --> 01:00:05,519
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
